streaming_chunk5_peak_rss_2026-05-18.tsv
========================================

Date:        2026-05-18T11:27:14Z
Hostname:    lilith
CPU:         AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (32 threads), 128 GB RAM
jj change:   wkrkuwovlnxr (per-region quant_field+mask1x1+gaborish)
Parent:      78f803f4 (chunk-3 per-region loop driver)

Reproducer
----------
  cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop' \
    --example bench_buffering_rss
  for v in full buffered streaming; do
    for chunk5 in "" "1"; do
      JXL_STREAMING_CHUNK5=$chunk5 /usr/bin/time -v \
        ./target/release/examples/bench_buffering_rss $v 3072 3072
    done
  done

Columns
-------
  variant       Buffering enum mapping (full=FullBuffered, buffered=BufferedOutput, streaming=FullStreaming)
  chunk5        Dispatch flag: "off" = chunk-3 whole-image precompute, "on" = chunk-5 per-region precompute
  width,height  Image dimensions (px)
  bytes         Encoded JXL bytes
  wall_s        End-to-end wall-clock encode (8 threads)
  peak_rss_kb   Max resident set size from /usr/bin/time -v (kB)

Findings
--------
1. **Bytes are bit-identical across every (variant, chunk5) cell**
   at 3072×3072 d=1.0. The chunk-5 per-region dispatch produces the
   exact same bitstream as the chunk-3 whole-image dispatch — the
   bounded FP drift (1-256 ULPs on individual mask1x1 / gaborish
   values) is absorbed by the downstream quantization and AC
   strategy thresholding.

2. **Peak RSS is ~unchanged across every cell** (1.63 GiB ± 3 MB).
   The chunk-5 per-region functions write into the same whole-image-
   sized output buffers (quant_field / masking / mask1x1 / xyb_x/y/b)
   that downstream consumers (rate_control / butteraugli loop /
   encode_from_precomputed) expect. **Memory savings require chunk 4
   (per-DC-group encode_dc_group split)** so the loop driver can
   drop the per-region precompute output AS SOON AS the
   corresponding bitstream section is emitted.

   Chunk 5 is the structural prereq — per-region functions
   are validated and wired through a dispatch — but the load-bearing
   memory win lands when chunk 6 wires `Buffering::BufferedOutput`
   and `Buffering::FullStreaming` to a real per-DC-group encode loop
   that drops state immediately.

Honest-stop disposition (per chunk-5 user spec)
-----------------------------------------------
The user gate "**Target: 2-4× peak-RSS reduction at 4K**" is NOT
hit by this chunk in isolation. Per the honest-stop condition:

  > If memory measurement doesn't hit 2× minimum: investigate.
  > The 24 B/pixel whole-image working set should shrink by ~7-8×
  > when only one DC group's worth lives at a time, so 2× should
  > be conservative.

Investigation result: the bench measures the FULL encode pipeline,
not just the per-region precompute phase. The full pipeline currently
holds (whole-image XYB planes + whole-image pre-gaborish snapshot +
whole-image quant_field / masking / mask1x1 + whole-image cfl_map /
ac_strategy + accumulated bitstream sections + butteraugli scratch
buffers). The chunk-5 per-region path replaces the whole-image
*precompute* but the *output assembly buffers* still live at
whole-image scope because every downstream consumer
(`rate_control::adjust_quant_field`, butteraugli loop,
`encode_from_precomputed`) expects whole-image inputs.

Closing the loop on RSS requires either:
  (a) chunk 4 + chunk 6: split `encode_from_precomputed` so each DC
      group's section is emitted (and its assembly buffer freed)
      before the next DC group runs.
  (b) An out-of-band streaming mode where rate_control / butteraugli
      loop are skipped entirely (BufferedOutput is documented to
      lose a small amount of compression density in libjxl too).

Either path is the chunk-6/7 work item described in the porting
plan memory `libjxl_streaming_refactor_porting_plan_2026-05-18.md`.

Hash-lock / RD regression
-------------------------
Both gated paths (chunk5=off and chunk5=on):
  - `cargo test --test hash_lock_features`: 36/36 byte-identical
  - `cargo test --test buffering_dispatch`: 4/4 byte-identical
  - `just rd-regression` (18 cells): all within ±3% size,
    ±5% butteraugli, ±1.0 SSIM2 — chunk5=on path actually marginally
    *improves* size (0.0% to 0.3% smaller) on every test image.
  - `just rd-regression-hd` (6 cells): all within quality thresholds.

Per-region unit tests
---------------------
  vardct::adaptive_quant::tests::test_per_region_quant_field_matches_whole_image
    — exact byte-identity (multi-region 12×8 block assembly = whole image)
  vardct::adaptive_quant::tests::test_per_region_mask1x1_matches_whole_image
    — max 8 ULP drift on individual pixels (PAD=3 closes the
      kernel-clamp divergence at interior region boundaries)
  vardct::gaborish::tests::test_per_region_gaborish_matches_whole_image
    — max 256 ULP drift on individual pixels (SIMD-boundary lane
      assignment + scalar-vs-SIMD-row dispatch in the whole-image
      kernel's top/bottom rows differ from the per-region path)

End-to-end byte-identity at 3072×3072 (bench above) demonstrates the
per-function FP drift does not propagate to bitstream divergence.
